.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/duscope/config.toml
The configuration file
.RI ( ~/.config/duscope/config.toml
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset), or the file
.B \-\-config
or
.B DUSCOPE_CONFIG
names.
.B [defaults]
sets the defaults of
.BR threads ,
.BR theme ,
.BR color_by ,
.BR format ,
.BR limit ,
.BR size ,
.BR attrs ,
.BR clones ,
.B index_dir
and
.BR max_age ,
under the flags' names; a flag or its environment variable wins over it.
.B [excludes] patterns
lists
.B \-\-exclude
patterns every scan leaves out;
.B [classes] extra
and
.B [caches] extra
name tables merged over the built\-in ones. Relative paths are the file's
directory's. A
.I .duscope.toml
inside a scanned tree is never read.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/duscope/scans/<id>.db
A saved scan, written by
.B scan \-\-save
or by a list verb that found none holding its path:
one SQLite file, mode 0600, written once and never changed
.RI ( ~/Library/Caches/duscope
on macOS and
.I ~/.cache/duscope
elsewhere when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset;
.B \-\-index\-dir
or
.B DUSCOPE_INDEX_DIR
names another directory).
.B scans
lists them,
.B scans \-\-prune
removes the old ones, and
.B \-\-scan
names one; an index file outside the directory is read only when
.B \-\-trust
names it. The directory and its
.I scans
are mode 0700; duscope warns when they or an index file are open to
other users. Its tables are described in
.I docs/index-format.md
in the source distribution.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/duscope/handle.key
The key that signs
.BR "explain \-\-json" 's
handles: 32 random bytes, mode 0600, made on first use. A key that is a
symbolic link, another user's, or readable by others signs nothing;
deleting it invalidates every handle given out.
.TP
.I theme.toml
A theme for
.B \-\-theme
or
.BR DUSCOPE_THEME :
thirteen role colours, seven class colours, a ten\-colour cycle and a
five\-step age ramp, each
.BR #rrggbb .
.TP
.I classes.toml
A classes table for
.BR "by\-type \-\-classes" ,
merged over the built\-in one:
.B [ext]
maps an extension to a class,
.B [dir]
a directory name or glob.
.TP
.I ignore files
Gitignore\-syntax files for
.BR \-\-ignore\-from ,
negations included; and plain pattern files for
.BR \-\-exclude\-from .
.PP
The formats are in
.I docs/rules.md
in the source distribution.
